---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CopyEmail from '../components/CopyEmail.astro';
import { site, experience, education } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/content';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" active="About" description="Muntaha Kamal’s path from data science at Micron to AI engineering at Tata Electronics, building machine learning, deep learning, and LLM applications.">
  <header class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Background</div><h1>About me.</h1><p>My work brings together data science, deep learning, and LLM application development.</p></header>
  <div class="about-grid" data-pagefind-body>
    <div class="about-prose">
      <p>After graduating from IIT Delhi in 2022, I joined Micron as a data scientist, progressing from Data Scientist I to II. My work covered machine learning for NAND memory reliability and statistical analysis of manufacturing test data. I developed anomaly analysis to surface local error-count variation below static limits and prioritized recurring outliers for interactive investigation. I also co-developed a shared reliability platform, owning reusable, tested Python modeling-workflow modules, visualization, and evaluation, with peer review of code and design decisions.</p>
      <p>Alongside model development, I built tools that helped engineers use the results. A decision-support model explained its recommendations and withheld them when confidence was low, while engineers retained final approval. That workflow shortened review turnaround by about 14 days. I also co-developed a cloud data and inference pipeline that reduced combined modeling and data-engineering effort by approximately 50%.</p>
      <p>I joined Tata Electronics as an AI engineer in December 2025. There, I built a GraphRAG-based learning platform that turns technical documentation into department-specific learning modules, selecting the retrieval approach and developing ingestion pipelines for text, tables, and images. I changed retrieval to keep evidence tied to selected documents, including when those documents shared entities. Five months of training in Taiwan also gave me practical context on fab systems, wafer movement, and production data.</p>
      <p>Outside work, I build <a href={withBase('/projects/')}>independent projects</a> to explore other engineering problems. CommitEcho grew from the difficulty of recovering why code changed during long-running projects with coding agents. My other projects explore LLM applications and circuit analysis.</p>
      <div class="link-group"><a class="text-link" href={withBase(site.resume)}>Download résumé ↓</a><CopyEmail /></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-sidebar"><h2>Areas of work</h2><p>Machine learning, deep learning, computer vision, LLM applications—including RAG and GraphRAG—and data workflows.</p><h2>Education</h2><p><strong>{education.institution}</strong><br/>{education.degree}<br/>{education.period}</p><h2>Elsewhere</h2><p><a class="text-link" href={site.github}>GitHub ↗</a><br/><a class="text-link" href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a></p></aside>
  </div>
  <section class="section" style="margin-top:50px" aria-labelledby="experience-title" data-pagefind-body><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="experience-title">Experience</h2></div>{experience.map(job => <article class="experience-row"><div><time>{job.period}</time></div><div><h3>{job.company}</h3><div class="role">{job.role}</div><p>{job.description}</p><ul>{job.highlights.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul></div></article>)}</section>
</BaseLayout>
